1
00:00:00,933 --> 00:00:01,567
<i>She hid in a different
syndicate.</i>

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:02,700
<i>It seems we have no other choice</i>

3
00:00:02,833 --> 00:00:05,000
<i>but to break into that
Godfather's villa.</i>

4
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:09,000
<i>I'd like to ask
for your husband's help.</i>

5
00:00:09,133 --> 00:00:12,800
<i>One of my employees,
her husband, is in jail.</i>

6
00:00:12,933 --> 00:00:16,633
<i>His name is former
Major Miguel Delgado.</i>

7
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:17,800
<i> I'll try to see what I can do.</i>

8
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:20,100
<i>Do you know Vicente Alcala's
house?</i>

9
00:00:20,233 --> 00:00:22,967
<i>The events team sent me
for his party.</i>

10
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:24,667
<i> Joey, you're not included.</i>

11
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,100
<i>It's not good when there's
a woman.</i>

12
00:00:26,233 --> 00:00:27,833
<i> You might get emotional again.</i>

13
00:00:27,967 --> 00:00:29,467
<i>What's your real issue with me?</i>

14
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,867
<i>Is it because I'm a failure,
or because I'm emotional?</i>

15
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,133
<i> Or because I'm a woman?</i>

16
00:00:33,267 --> 00:00:34,900
<i>Maybe she'll find out something
about the organization.</i>

17
00:00:35,067 --> 00:00:35,933
<i> Should I work on it?</i>

18
00:00:36,067 --> 00:00:38,067
<i>No, as long as she doesn't know,</i>

19
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:40,167
<i>we can use her against
his husband.</i>

20
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,833
<i>And that's how we burn him
slowly.</i>

21
00:00:42,967 --> 00:00:45,600
<i>By the way, can I ask you
for a favor?</i>

22
00:00:45,733 --> 00:00:47,200
<i>It's not because you're a police
officer outside,</i>

23
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:48,600
<i> you're important here.</i>

24
00:00:48,733 --> 00:00:50,300
<i> Andrew, join us!</i>

25
00:00:50,433 --> 00:00:52,267
<i>Alcohol is dangerous for robots
because they'll get rusty,</i>

26
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:56,200
<i>and they'll lose feelings
even more.</i>

27
00:00:56,333 --> 00:00:57,400
<i> Game.</i>

28
00:00:57,533 --> 00:00:58,833
<i> Give me that.</i>

29
00:00:58,967 --> 00:00:59,933
<i> Why? What do you think?</i>

30
00:01:00,067 --> 00:01:02,333
<i>I can't drink because
I'm a woman, right?</i>

31
00:01:02,467 --> 00:01:05,400
<i>- Shot! Shot!
- Just take it easy.</i>

32
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:07,200
<i> That's enough, you're drunk.</i>

33
00:01:07,367 --> 00:01:12,600
<i>What do I need to do so you
don't treat me like a child?</i>

34
00:01:12,733 --> 00:01:14,133
<i> Tell me!</i>

35
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:44,733
What is this?

36
00:01:44,867 --> 00:01:46,467
What are you doing to Joey?

37
00:01:48,767 --> 00:01:49,800
You animal!

38
00:01:49,933 --> 00:01:51,600
You're taking advantage of her
because she's drunk!

39
00:01:51,733 --> 00:01:52,600
- Wait.
- What's your problem?

40
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:54,767
You got it wrong.
I don't have a problem.

41
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,767
Then explain.
Why are you on top of her?

42
00:01:57,900 --> 00:01:59,500
She pulled me.

43
00:01:59,633 --> 00:02:01,267
I fell on her.

44
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,500
That's it. Accident.

45
00:02:03,633 --> 00:02:06,033
Is that true? Is that true,
Joey?

46
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:07,600
True.

47
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:16,933
Joey...

48
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:23,800
Did you kiss her?

49
00:02:27,467 --> 00:02:28,533
Me?

50
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:31,767
Paranoid.

51
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:35,333
Wanna drink some more?

52
00:02:35,467 --> 00:02:36,333
Okay.

53
00:02:41,933 --> 00:02:44,867
You're drunk!

54
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,500
You've outdone the guys bumming
around in our area.

55
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,433
Have some water.

56
00:03:08,133 --> 00:03:11,567
Am I really a failure, Peter?

57
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:14,700
What? No!

58
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,067
Don't believe Andrew.

59
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:23,100
Boss Budol is his name,
that's why he's like that!

60
00:03:23,267 --> 00:03:25,533
Don't believe that, don't.

61
00:03:25,667 --> 00:03:33,000
- Never, never. Never say...
- Boss Budol.

62
00:03:33,133 --> 00:03:35,033
You called him that.

63
00:03:37,233 --> 00:03:38,333
What?

64
00:03:38,467 --> 00:03:40,133
Boss Budol...

65
00:03:41,833 --> 00:03:43,067
- Boss Budol...
- You know...

66
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,567
You're really my best friend.

67
00:03:46,967 --> 00:03:48,800
Thank you.

68
00:03:48,933 --> 00:03:53,500
At least, you, you know
I'm not a failure.

69
00:03:53,633 --> 00:03:57,200
- Right?
- No. You're not a failure.

70
00:03:58,833 --> 00:04:00,633
You're not a failure.

71
00:04:00,767 --> 00:04:02,700
You're so good.

72
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:05,867
You're so brave.
You're even braver than me.

73
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,200
You know that?
That's why we're not the same.

74
00:04:09,333 --> 00:04:11,700
You're here! This is you,
and this is me.

75
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,633
There you are.

76
00:04:16,767 --> 00:04:18,200
Tall.

77
00:04:18,333 --> 00:04:20,300
My height.

78
00:04:24,533 --> 00:04:28,600
But you know,
even though we're different,

79
00:04:30,133 --> 00:04:33,167
I won't give up. No!

80
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:34,367
Because...

81
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:37,533
nothing, that's how it is...

82
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,567
I love you.

83
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,567
I have a chance, don't I?

84
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:00,067
Buddy, a letter?

85
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:03,500
A letter to my family.
But I never sent it.

86
00:05:03,667 --> 00:05:06,567
They changed their address.
I don't know how to find them.

87
00:05:07,933 --> 00:05:10,633
I know I don't value here,

88
00:05:10,767 --> 00:05:14,500
but I have a lot of connections
outside.

89
00:05:14,633 --> 00:05:16,700
I can make them find
your family.

90
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:24,667
What do you need from Trigger?
Are you going to ask for help?

91
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:27,833
He's cunning
and a double-crosser.

92
00:05:27,967 --> 00:05:30,533
I just need some information
from him.

93
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,967
Maybe...

94
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:42,800
angels are good at pretending
to be demons like him.

95
00:05:42,933 --> 00:05:45,333
But those guys have weaknesses,
too.

96
00:06:05,467 --> 00:06:07,400
Don't.

97
00:06:17,467 --> 00:06:20,867
Let's drink more.

98
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,100
More shots.

99
00:06:25,633 --> 00:06:27,667
That's enough.
We're out of alcohol.

100
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,333
You're not allowed
to drink anymore.

101
00:06:29,467 --> 00:06:31,467
Am I not allowed?

102
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:35,300
Why am I not allowed?
Are you the boss?

103
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:39,633
Yes, and, I'm ordering you
to go to sleep.

104
00:06:43,067 --> 00:06:44,367
I don't want to!

105
00:06:47,133 --> 00:06:50,533
You're arrogant. You're perfect.

106
00:06:51,567 --> 00:06:52,933
Really?

107
00:06:56,133 --> 00:06:57,867
You're perfect.

108
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:00,967
Hardworking.

109
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,733
Brave.

110
00:07:06,033 --> 00:07:07,933
Handsome.

111
00:07:11,733 --> 00:07:12,933
I'm handsome?

112
00:07:14,567 --> 00:07:16,867
Yes...

113
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,700
Boss Idol, right?

114
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:24,933
That's why...

115
00:07:25,067 --> 00:07:27,033
That's why what?

116
00:07:27,167 --> 00:07:28,967
That's why...

117
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,933
Okay.

118
00:07:42,733 --> 00:07:46,733
Hon, what will I say
to Clarissa?

119
00:07:46,867 --> 00:07:50,633
You know, something that could
give her hope.

120
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,767
I already talked to a friend
at the RTC.

121
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,233
The case is serious.

122
00:08:05,367 --> 00:08:07,733
Murder, non-bailable.

123
00:08:07,867 --> 00:08:09,600
But they say they can consider

124
00:08:09,733 --> 00:08:12,333
a motion for reconsideration
of bail.

125
00:08:12,467 --> 00:08:14,533
Especially if there
are lapses in evidence or,

126
00:08:14,667 --> 00:08:16,067
mitigating factors.

127
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:24,867
Thank you, Hon.

128
00:08:26,867 --> 00:08:32,733
But I hope, don't think
I'm just using you.

129
00:08:32,867 --> 00:08:33,900
Too late.

130
00:08:34,033 --> 00:08:35,200
Almost there.

131
00:08:38,033 --> 00:08:39,833
But you know, Hon,

132
00:08:39,967 --> 00:08:42,600
seriously, I just feel
for Clarissa.

133
00:08:42,733 --> 00:08:46,600
She's kind, and honestly,

134
00:08:46,733 --> 00:08:50,500
it's a shame because she's smart
and competent.

135
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:53,733
If she weren't going through
something

136
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:57,000
so difficult in her life,
I know...

137
00:08:57,133 --> 00:08:59,000
I know she could do more.

138
00:08:59,133 --> 00:09:00,767
That's why I want to meet her.

139
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:03,600
I want to hear her story
firsthand,

140
00:09:03,733 --> 00:09:08,533
so we know what and who we're
letting ourselves in for.

141
00:09:08,667 --> 00:09:13,333
Okay, okay, I'll set it up,
okay?

142
00:09:13,467 --> 00:09:14,733
Thank you.

143
00:09:59,333 --> 00:10:03,567
<i>- Joey, you eat first, so...
- No need, Peter. I'll do it.</i>

144
00:10:03,733 --> 00:10:05,033
<i> I can do it.</i>

145
00:10:05,167 --> 00:10:09,833
<i>Just because I'm a girl,
I'm all emotions, right?</i>

146
00:10:09,967 --> 00:10:11,467
<i> You want water, Joey?</i>

147
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:14,833
<i>Thank you, Jin Ho.
You're so sweet.</i>

148
00:10:14,967 --> 00:10:17,267
<i>You really care
about my feelings.</i>

149
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:23,500
<i>You should analyze the situation
first before you say anything.</i>

150
00:10:23,633 --> 00:10:27,567
<i>It's more important to analyze
your egos first.</i>

151
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:28,367
<i> So...</i>

152
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,300
<i> so I have issues with my ego?</i>

153
00:10:30,433 --> 00:10:32,200
<i> Why? Did it affect you?</i>

154
00:10:37,333 --> 00:10:38,400
<i> Just wait.</i>

155
00:10:38,533 --> 00:10:41,133
<i>There will come a moment,
a crack in the wall,</i>

156
00:10:41,267 --> 00:10:44,100
<i>a look, then you'll suddenly
realize...</i>

157
00:10:44,233 --> 00:10:47,300
<i>why does this girl matter a lot?</i>

158
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:08,767
Here.

159
00:11:10,733 --> 00:11:12,167
What's this?

160
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:16,500
Coconut water for hydration
and hangover.

161
00:11:16,633 --> 00:11:20,033
So you don't look like a zombie
all day.

162
00:11:26,367 --> 00:11:28,033
Water first.

163
00:11:28,167 --> 00:11:29,467
Thank you.

164
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,667
My head hurts.

165
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:56,367
What happened last night?
I blacked out.

166
00:11:58,467 --> 00:12:00,667
Don't you remember
what I said to you?

167
00:12:01,967 --> 00:12:03,567
What did you say?

168
00:12:07,467 --> 00:12:09,833
I don't remember what I said.
I guess it's not important.

169
00:12:09,967 --> 00:12:10,933
It's just nothing.

170
00:12:11,067 --> 00:12:12,467
- What is it?
- Drink it.

171
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,100
Maybe...

172
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:15,133
Maybe you'll remember.

173
00:12:15,300 --> 00:12:20,367
So you don't remember what you
said to me last night either?

174
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,833
I don't remember anything.
What did I say?

175
00:12:22,967 --> 00:12:25,267
I said nothing.

176
00:13:22,567 --> 00:13:25,233
How sure are you
that you'll find my family?

177
00:13:26,867 --> 00:13:28,733
Even though I'm no longer
in the service,

178
00:13:28,867 --> 00:13:30,500
I still have a lot
of connections.

179
00:13:31,733 --> 00:13:36,200
My fellow cops,
government people, politicians,

180
00:13:36,333 --> 00:13:37,900
even criminals.

181
00:13:39,633 --> 00:13:42,533
I've talked to Trigger.
He agreed to what you wanted.

182
00:13:43,900 --> 00:13:44,700
Hey!

183
00:13:46,067 --> 00:13:47,700
Let's move to Building A!

184
00:13:50,067 --> 00:13:51,467
Let's talk later.

185
00:13:58,300 --> 00:14:00,633
So later, I will head out.

186
00:14:00,767 --> 00:14:03,833
I will try to get access
to their office

187
00:14:03,967 --> 00:14:06,033
and find the guest list.

188
00:14:06,167 --> 00:14:09,333
And I can do it on my own.

189
00:14:09,467 --> 00:14:11,500
I don't need a chaperone.

190
00:14:11,633 --> 00:14:14,133
Okay, just make sure that
my name is on that list.

191
00:14:16,167 --> 00:14:18,500
Didn't we talk about this, Joey?

192
00:14:18,633 --> 00:14:21,267
- You're not coming.
- And why?

193
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:23,967
Did I agree to what you wanted?
What?

194
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:26,733
You're having trouble with me
being a woman again, aren't you?

195
00:14:26,867 --> 00:14:28,367
There we go.

196
00:14:28,533 --> 00:14:31,167
Please, Andrew, I can fight too.

197
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:33,200
I'm a black belter.

198
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:40,900
Okay.

199
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,367
Thank you for agreeing
to talk to me.

200
00:14:56,667 --> 00:14:58,333
I just wanted to...

201
00:15:15,867 --> 00:15:16,733
I don't want trouble.

202
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:19,533
I just want to know something.

203
00:15:19,667 --> 00:15:23,067
What if you betray me like what
you did to your best friend,

204
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,767
Major Aglipay?

205
00:15:24,900 --> 00:15:26,700
I'm not his traitor.

206
00:15:26,833 --> 00:15:29,367
He betrayed me,
that's why I'm locked up here.

207
00:15:30,633 --> 00:15:33,133
I'm not part of their syndicate.

208
00:15:33,267 --> 00:15:35,200
And you're fooling me, right?

209
00:15:45,833 --> 00:15:47,233
<i> Open this door!</i>

210
00:15:49,267 --> 00:15:51,067
Hey, what are you doing there?

211
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,167
Back to the cell.

212
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,000
You're lucky now.

213
00:16:09,767 --> 00:16:11,067
Clarissa...

214
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:11,867
Yes?

215
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,633
I have good news for you.

216
00:16:13,767 --> 00:16:15,600
I've already talked
to my husband

217
00:16:15,733 --> 00:16:18,433
about your husband's case.

218
00:16:18,567 --> 00:16:19,867
Really?

219
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,300
Yes, but he wants to know more,

220
00:16:22,433 --> 00:16:23,667
that's why he wants to talk
to you.

221
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:26,067
But he's just in Hong Kong
for a conference.

222
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:29,200
But when he arrives,
I'll introduce you to him.

223
00:16:29,333 --> 00:16:30,967
Okay, Ma'am.

224
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:33,600
Thank you very much, Ma'am.

225
00:16:33,733 --> 00:16:36,867
I don't know how to repay you.

226
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,333
Of course, we help each other
here.

227
00:16:40,467 --> 00:16:42,233
Excuse me, Ma'am.

228
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:48,167
An invitation has arrived
from one of our target sponsors.

229
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:59,167
It's such short notice.

230
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:00,633
Should I decline?

231
00:17:00,767 --> 00:17:02,700
Well, I hope Tomas is here.

232
00:17:02,833 --> 00:17:04,833
It's more strategic that way,
right?

233
00:17:04,967 --> 00:17:05,700
Yes.

234
00:17:05,833 --> 00:17:08,567
Ma'am, excuse me.

235
00:17:09,767 --> 00:17:15,300
Well, it would be a waste
of an opportunity

236
00:17:15,467 --> 00:17:18,600
if you don't go for it.

237
00:17:18,733 --> 00:17:24,867
Also, we've been courting
that sponsor for a long time.

238
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,267
Well, you're right.

239
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:30,933
We cannot miss this opportunity,
right?

240
00:17:32,667 --> 00:17:34,167
Okay.

241
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:36,467
Confirm my attendance, okay?

242
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:38,833
- Okay, Ma'am.
- Thank you.

243
00:17:38,967 --> 00:17:40,667
Joey, you don't have
to do this anymore.

244
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:42,867
I need to, so we'll finally
know.

245
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,367
This is in your favor!

246
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,100
The area is wide enough
and if you get tired,

247
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:47,567
you can run, right?

248
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:49,800
Can you hear what she says?

249
00:17:49,933 --> 00:17:51,133
You're laughing there.

250
00:17:51,267 --> 00:17:53,933
You go first, so your giggles
will disappear!

251
00:17:54,067 --> 00:17:55,367
Let's go, Brother!

252
00:17:59,033 --> 00:18:01,000
- Don't, don't.
- You're so weak!

253
00:18:01,133 --> 00:18:03,933
- Just stand there!
- I'm not yet ready.

254
00:18:04,067 --> 00:18:06,800
- Let's go! I'll help you.
- Yes, I'll do it.

255
00:18:16,267 --> 00:18:17,267
I got you.

256
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:18,267
Are you sure?

257
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:19,100
Yeah.

258
00:18:53,167 --> 00:18:58,100
Joey, does being a black belter
help you with this?

259
00:18:58,267 --> 00:18:59,067
Remember.

260
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:02,600
Your enemies are gun smugglers.

261
00:19:17,167 --> 00:19:18,867
And check again.

262
00:19:24,667 --> 00:19:25,767
Your turn.

263
00:19:41,167 --> 00:19:42,367
Keep going.

264
00:19:50,967 --> 00:19:52,133
Good job!

265
00:19:53,033 --> 00:19:55,100
Wow Joey. You're fast.

266
00:19:56,900 --> 00:19:59,500
Maybe you've forgotten that
my father is a police officer?

267
00:20:01,567 --> 00:20:06,200
But we'll only use that when
were at a disadvantage.

268
00:20:06,333 --> 00:20:08,533
It's always good to be ready.

269
00:20:08,667 --> 00:20:11,167
And it's even better
if you can shoot.

270
00:20:16,467 --> 00:20:19,133
Okay, Joey, game.

271
00:20:26,733 --> 00:20:27,867
Okay...

272
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:33,167
One foot forward for balance.
Bend your knees.

273
00:20:39,133 --> 00:20:40,800
Firm grip.

274
00:20:40,933 --> 00:20:43,033
Firm.

275
00:20:43,167 --> 00:20:44,767
Don't lock your elbows.

276
00:20:46,467 --> 00:20:47,700
Eyes up.

277
00:20:49,233 --> 00:20:50,500
Breathe.

278
00:20:50,633 --> 00:20:51,900
Steady.

279
00:21:10,767 --> 00:21:12,233
Game, you can do it.

280
00:21:24,367 --> 00:21:26,300
Joey, control that...

281
00:21:27,667 --> 00:21:29,000
Control this.

282
00:21:30,667 --> 00:21:31,900
Don't jerk...

283
00:21:34,033 --> 00:21:37,600
and keep aiming after every
shot.

284
00:21:51,667 --> 00:21:53,367
Go, Joey. You can do it!

285
00:21:54,667 --> 00:21:56,000
It's my hair.

286
00:21:59,933 --> 00:22:00,967
Give me that.

287
00:22:02,533 --> 00:22:03,933
Joey, this is...

288
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,000
Not bad.

289
00:22:49,967 --> 00:22:51,367
Five, why...

290
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:52,367
How did you do that?

291
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,767
Expert....

292
00:23:10,367 --> 00:23:13,333
Joey, can we talk?

293
00:23:13,467 --> 00:23:15,700
Braganza has a target here
in Luzon.

294
00:23:15,833 --> 00:23:17,900
We need to find out what
they're up to, Matias.

295
00:23:18,033 --> 00:23:20,067
It looks like the transaction
will happen there.

296
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,067
Golda.

297
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:22,933
Long live the king!

298
00:23:23,100 --> 00:23:24,900
Has my gift arrived yet?

299
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:32,067
Joey, be careful.

300
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:34,767
If something goes wrong,
just walk away.
